odules and heavy black-and-lime shoes. <Picture 3> is the approved game-menu composition, UI layout, typography hierarchy, color system and character-position reference. Preserve the red, black, ivory-white and restrained neon-lime palette, diagonal comic panels, halftone patterns, dry brush shapes, angular menu cards and clear commercial game-interface hierarchy.\n\nIdentity and position lock: ALIANG is PLAYER 1 and always remains on the left. JUN is PLAYER 2 and always remains on the right. Never exchange their faces, names, hairstyles, clothes, body proportions, accessories or screen positions. Keep both characters as compact premium stylized 3D figures integrated into an original high-contrast red-black-white comic interface. Do not copy any existing commercial game logo, character, symbol or exact branded menu.\n\n[Shot 1] 00:00.000–00:02.500 — Approved cooperative game menu. Begin from the visual composition established by <Picture 3>. Stable high-angle 16:9 wide shot with a very slight forward push. ALIANG sits on the left and JUN sits on the right, both clearly visible and naturally integrated into the graphic menu. They perform only restrained idle motion: subtle breathing, one natural blink and a slight shift of attention toward the highlighted menu. Preserve the exact visible UI strings: the title “MECHANICAL ANOMALY”; the upper-left player cards “PLAYER 1”, “ALIANG”, “READY”, and “PLAYER 2”, “JUN”, “READY”; the right-side menu “START NEW GAME”, “CONTINUE”, “SETTINGS”, “EXIT GAME”. “CONTINUE” remains the dominant highlighted button. A white angular focus frame slides onto “CONTINUE”, the red border compresses once and the small neon-lime confirmation marker illuminates. Keep all text sharp, correctly spelled and unobstructed.\n\n[Shot 2] 00:02.500–00:05.000 — ALIANG equipment activation. The right-side menu folds into flat diagonal panels while the camera smoothly pushes toward ALIANG on the left. JUN remains visible on the right in the background and retains her identity without deformation. A compact black, ivory and neon-lime equipment panel slides in beside ALIANG and displays only the approved strings “PLAYER 1”, “ALIANG” and “MECHANICAL GLOVE”. ALIANG raises his existing mechanical right glove. Its outer plates separate slightly along established seams, internal lime status lights activate sequentially from wrist to fingertips, and the articulated fingers complete exactly one controlled open-and-close diagnostic cycle. The glove remains part of his original costume; do not replace his arm, enlarge the hand or introduce a weapon.\n\n[Shot 3] 00:05.000–00:07.500 — JUN scanning action. The camera makes a smooth lateral transition to JUN on the right while ALIANG remains visible on the left in the background, lowering his activated glove. A red, black and ivory scan panel appears beside JUN and displays only “PLAYER 2”, “JUN” and “SYSTEM SCAN”. JUN lifts the small device already associated with her costume and performs one visible scanning action. A restrained red angular scan frame travels once across the interface and both player cards. Small lime indicators confirm ALIANG and JUN separately without merging their profiles. JUN’s hat, long gray ponytail, pink-red hair strands, jacket patches and creature-shaped accessory remain unchanged.\n\n[Shot 4] 00:07.500–00:09.500 — Cooperative confirmation. Return to a stable centered two-character composition with ALIANG on the left and JUN on the right. Their two equipment panels slide toward the center and combine into one angular shared button reading “CONFIRM CONFIG”. A cursor moves onto the button and presses it once. ALIANG places his activated mechanical glove against the left confirmation zone while JUN places her scanner against the right confirmation zone. Two distinct signals—neon lime from ALIANG and controlled red from JUN—travel inward and meet at the center. The button changes visibly from idle to confirmed. Both characters exchange one brief coordinated glance; no celebration, dancing or additional gestures.\n\n[Shot 5] 00:09.500–00:11.000 — Loading transition. The interface clears into a graphic loading state without a hard cut. A single horizontal bar appears along the lower center with the exact word “LOADING”. The left half fills with ALIANG’s neon-lime accent and the right half fills with JUN’s red accent, advancing clearly from 0% to 100%. The flat red, black and ivory comic panels begin transforming continuously into physical urban surfaces: diagonal shapes become mechanical walkways, halftone fields become textured walls, black brush areas become alley shadows and red graphic lines become illuminated route markers. Do not conceal the transformation with smoke, flashes or full-screen effects.\n\n[Shot 6] 00:11.000–00:15.000 — Entering the mechanical anomaly city. At 100%, ALIANG and JUN rise together while preserving their original costumes and body proportions. The camera lowers smoothly and moves behind them into a stable third-person cooperative viewpoint. ALIANG remains on the left with his mechanical glove naturally lowered; JUN remains on the right holding her compact scanner. They take several coordinated steps into an original mechanical city built from the established graphic language: layered industrial walkways, angular machinery, red route signs without readable commercial text, black alley openings, ivory structural panels, restrained lime status lights and halftone-inspired environmental textures. A minimal HUD fades in. The lower-left displays two separate readable status labels, “ALIANG” and “JUN”, using their assigned colors. One shared objective marker appears ahead. End with both characters standing side by side facing the mechanical city, identities and silhouettes fully readable.\n\noverall_soundscape: Quiet game-menu ambience, one restrained hover sound and one clear menu-confirmation click; precise lightweight mechanical plate movements and sequential electronic ticks for ALIANG’s glove; one short scanner sweep and two identity-confirmation tones for JUN; a solid cooperative confirmation impact; a rising loading tone that resolves exactly at 100%; then mechanical-city ambience, distant machinery, soft route-signal pulses, synchronized footsteps and one subtle HUD activation sound. No dialogue.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Original high-energy instrumental game-intro rhythm using dry percussion, restrained electric bass, clipped brass-like accents and angular electronic hits. Synchronize major accents with the menu confirmation, glove activation, scan completion, cooperative confirmation and loading completion. Briefly reduce the arrangement during the loading transition, then return with a controlled final phrase as the two characters enter the city. Do not reproduce or imitate any existing game soundtrack or melody.\n\ncontinuity_constraints: Keep ALIANG as PLAYER 1 on the left and JUN as PLAYER 2 on the right throughout. Preserve their exact identity anchors, hairstyles, hats, facial features, outfits, accessories, body proportions and assigned colors from <Picture 1> and <Picture 2>. Use <Picture 3> only to preserve the approved composition, UI hierarchy, typography scale, palette and graphic language. Keep every visible string correctly spelled and limited to the explicitly approved text. Maintain a clean 16:9 commercial game presentation with stable readable UI. No third player, duplicated character, identity swap, username swap, merged bodies, identical body proportions, missing accessories, costume redesign, extra limbs, weapons, combat, split screen, hard cuts, random camera shake, excessive neon, purple palette, unreadable text, random letters, additional menu options, copied commercial game logo, branded interface or watermark."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "prompt"}, "name": "prompt", "label": "prompt", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "提示词"}], "flags": {}, "type": "CR Prompt Text", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [840.05218505859